at should lead to a plan.","input":{"hint":"arguments"},"source":"skill"},{"name":"skill:docker-isolate-worktree","description":"Add Docker isolation to a worktree you already created - renamed containers, offset ports, remapped mounts. Use when running parallel stacks across worktrees, or when containers clash between worktrees.","input":{"hint":"arguments"},"source":"skill"},{"name":"skill:find-skills","description":"Helps users discover and install agent skills when they ask questions like \"how do I do X\", \"find a skill for X\", \"is there a skill that can...\", or express interest in extending capabilities. This skill should be used when the user is looking for functionality that might exist as an installable skill.","input":{"hint":"arguments"},"source":"skill"},{"name":"skill:frontend-design","description":"Give UI a distinctive, intentional visual direction. Use when building new UI, restyling existing UI, choosing typography or aesthetic direction, or when a design looks templated and generic.","input":{"hint":"arguments"},"source":"skill"},{"name":"skill:going-to-sleep","description":"Hand off work to run autonomously while you are away. Use when the user says \"going to sleep\", \"I am going to bed\", \"work on this overnight\", \"stepping out\", \"back in a few hours\", or gives a goal plus a return time. Also the WAKE-UP handler - use on \"I am back\", \"good morning\", \"what happened overnight\", \"did you finish\".","input":{"hint":"arguments"},"source":"skill"},{"name":"skill:graphify","description":"Use for any question about a codebase, its architecture, file relationships, or project content — especially when graphify-out/ exists, where the question should be treated as a graphify query first. Turns any input (code, docs, papers, images, videos) into a persistent knowledge graph with god nodes, community detection, and query/path/explain tools.","input":{"hint":"arguments"},"source":"skill"},{"name":"skill:harness-relative-workspace-agent","description":"Pick the agent a spawned Superset workspace runs — spawn the SAME harness that is driving now (OMP → omp, opencode → opencode). Use whenever a skill or command says superset ws create --agent …, especially the ticket-* pipeline (ticket-kickoff, ticket-pr-split), which hardcodes opencode.","input":{"hint":"arguments"},"source":"skill"},{"name":"skill:harness-token-benchmark","description":"Benchmark coding harnesses (omp, claude code, opencode, pi, hermes) against each other on token cost, wall time and task success with the same model — including the runner traps that silently corrupt the numbers and the cache-write vs cache-read analysis that usually explains the cost gap.","input":{"hint":"arguments"},"source":"skill"},{"name":"skill:hook-development","description":"Write a plugin hook. Use when adding a PreToolUse, PostToolUse, Stop, SessionStart or UserPromptSubmit hook, validating or blocking tool calls, or setting up event-driven automation.","input":{"hint":"arguments"},"source":"skill"},{"name":"skill:ide-tooling","description":"Use the harness as an IDE instead of as a text editor — language-server rename/references/code actions, AST search and staged codemods, a real debugger with conditional breakpoints, CI run-watching, and checkpoint/rewind. Use when renaming or moving a symbol, hunting callers, writing a codemod, asking what a value is at runtime, waiting on CI, or when a symbol tool answers \"no language server found\" and the temptation is to fall back to sed, grep and print statements.","input":{"hint":"arguments"},"source":"skill"},{"name":"skill:jira-attachment-images","description":"Read the actual pixels of Jira ticket screenshots when the requirements live in images. Use when a ticket's corrections are in attachments, when getJiraIssue gives only attachment metadata, or when attachment download returns 403 / \"Failed to fetch\".","input":{"hint":"arguments"},"source":"skill"},{"name":"skill:jira-ticket-authoring","description":"Read 