t never delivered is not marked done: the agent has not seen it.\n *67│- **Working and Done stay inside one review round.** Reopening an ended session records the last\n  68│  take so far as `session.closed_delivery_seq`, and neither stamp lands on an entry delivered at or\n  69│  before it. A note `lavish-axi end` left at Seen stays Seen: a later round's edit or reply is about\n  70│  that round's notes.\n    │...\n  79│\n *80│## UI\n  81│\n  82│Each sent user bubble gets a one-line receipt under its text: the three emoji of the Telegram ack\n *83│protocol this mirrors, 👀 Seen, 🛠️ Working, ✅ Done, each lighting up once its stamp exists and\n  84│shown greyed and dimmed until then, so the row always shows what is still to come. Every step\n  85│carries its label and time (or \"not yet\") as both `title` and `aria-label`, so hover and screen\n  86│readers say the word, not the glyph. Before 👀 lights, the row carries the honest reason from the\n    │...\n  92│\n *93│## CLI and API changes\n  94│\n  95│None required for the automatic path. `lavish-axi poll`, `reply`, and the `/api/*` routes keep their\n  96│shapes. Two guidance strings gain one sentence each: `reply --help` and the poll `--agent-reply` row\n *97│in README say that a reply marks every request delivered to you as Done.\n  98│\n *99│## Transcripts from before receipts\n 100│\n 101│The positional rule is only true for sessions the receipt code has written from the start. An\n 102│existing `state.json` holds sessions whose user entries no take ever stamped; read naively, the\n 103│first poll after an upgrade would mark months-old notes Seen today and the next reply would mark\n*104│them Done. `readState`, the one load path every operation shares, therefore marks every user entry\n 105│of a session that has no `delivery_seq` key at all as `receipt: \"none\"` and persists that at once,\n 106│before any take can run. Those entries are skipped by every stamp helper and render no receipt row:\n 107│nothing was observed about them, and an empty row would read as \"never seen\".\n 108│\n*109│## Open issues for Igor\n 110│\n*111│- **A progress reply reads as Done.** `poll --agent-reply \"still working on it\"` stamps Done on\n 112│  every delivered note, exactly as it already clears the session-wide Working state. If a progress\n 113│  channel is wanted, it is a reply flag that posts without concluding; not built here.\n 114│- **Working means \"the file changed\", not \"the agent is on your note\".** An agent editing the\n    │...\n 117│- **`lavish-axi end` leaves notes at Seen.** Ending says the agent is finished with the review, not\n*118│  that each note was handled, so Done is not stamped. Say if the board should treat it as Done.\n 119│\n*120│## Alternatives rejected\n 121│\n 122│- **An explicit `lavish-axi ack <file> --working` command.** It is a new duty for every agent and\n 123│  harness, and the file watcher already supplies the signal for the common case. The upgrade path, if\n 124│  a progress channel is wanted, is a reply flag that posts a message without concluding the round;\n*125│  today `poll --agent-reply \"still working\"` stamps Done, exactly as it already clears Working.\n 126│- **Stamping on the poll's HTTP 200.** The take is destructive and the response can fail to write;\n 127│  stamping before the write and reverting on restore keeps one source of truth (`state.json`) and\n 128│  avoids a second bookkeeping path.\n    │...\n 131│  shorter and provably equivalent.\n*132│- **Marking Done when the agent ends the session.** `lavish-axi end` says the agent is finished with\n 133│  the review, not that it handled each note. Those stay Seen.\n 134│- **Session-level only.** That is today's presence stream; it cannot answer \"did it see _this_\"."},"isError":false,"timestamp":1792426563674},"messageId":"msg-54"}
